---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import OfferCard from '../components/OfferCard.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="Legacy Session — IslandTwig Studios"
	description="A complimentary 30-45 minute conversation to uncover your organization's story, goals, and the right path forward for your identity."
	path="/legacy-session"
>
	<section class="lw-hero">
		<div class="content">
			<div class="hero-grid">
				<div class="text-col">
					<span class="eyebrow">Legacy Session</span>
					<h1>Sports identities that <span class="accent-word">unite.</span></h1>
					<p class="lead">Custom brand identities for schools, teams, and leagues that inspire pride and strengthen community.</p>
					<p class="body">The Legacy Session is a complimentary 30&ndash;45 minute conversation to uncover where your organization is today, where you want to go next, and the right path to get there.</p>
					<a href="#start" class="btn btn-primary">Start Your Legacy Session</a>
				</div>
				<div class="hero-image">
					<img src="/images/case-studies/utah-hockey/mammoth-overview.jpeg" alt="Utah Mammoth concept: primary mark, wordmark, and jersey set in black, white, and red colorways" />
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- PROBLEM -->
	<section class="sec sec-cream">
		<svg class="stripe-mark" style="bottom: 20px; right: 20px; width: 220px; height: 220px; opacity: 0.45;" viewBox="0 0 200 200">
			<g transform="rotate(-22 100 100)">
				<rect x="10" y="40" width="120" height="14" rx="7" fill="var(--lw-accent)" opacity="0.25"/>
				<rect x="30" y="70" width="150" height="14" rx="7" fill="var(--lw-strong)" opacity="0.08"/>
				<rect x="0" y="100" width="90" height="14" rx="7" fill="var(--lw-accent)" opacity="0.15"/>
			</g>
		</svg>
		<div class="content">
			<div class="text-col">
				<p class="eyebrow">The problem</p>
				<h2 class="big">Your organization is more than a logo.</h2>
				<p class="body">Every team, school, and league has a story. It's built through traditions, people, memories, and moments that create a sense of belonging. But sometimes the identity representing that organization no longer reflects what it has become.</p>
				<ul class="pain-list">
					<li>Maybe your logo feels outdated.</li>
					<li>Maybe your merchandise doesn't create the excitement it should.</li>
					<li>Maybe your uniforms, social graphics, flyers, and other materials feel disconnected.</li>
					<li>Maybe you have built something special, but your identity doesn't give your community something they're proud to wear and represent.</li>
				</ul>
				<p class="body">A strong identity does more than look good. It helps unite players, connect fans, strengthen community pride, and create something people remember.</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- WHY THIS WORK MATTERS -->
	<section class="sec sec-soft">
		<div class="content">
			<div class="story-split">
				<div class="text-col">
					<p class="eyebrow">Why this work matters</p>
					<h2 class="big">I believe sports have the power to bring people together.</h2>
					<p class="body">Growing up, I saw firsthand how much a team's identity could mean. The colors, logo, and merchandise became part of the community. Families wore them. Players represented them. Fans rallied behind them.</p>
					<p class="body">Later, when I joined a club rugby team, I experienced the opposite. We had passion. We had pride. But our identity never reflected it. The logo and merchandise didn't capture what the organization meant to the people involved.</p>
					<p class="body">That experience stayed with me. Because a sports identity isn't just a graphic. It's the connection between an organization and the people who support it.</p>
					<p class="body">Today, I help schools, leagues, and sports organizations create identities that players wear with pride, fans rally behind, and communities remember.</p>
				</div>
				<div class="story-image">
					<img src="/images/legacy-session/rugby-team.jpg" alt="Nick's club rugby team posing together with their trophy and medals after a tournament win" />
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- Testimonials section hidden until there's a real client quote to put here.
	     Re-enable by uncommenting once one lands (Utah Flag or Hey Bright would do it).
	<section class="sec sec-cream">
		<div class="content">
			<p class="eyebrow" style="text-align:center;">Don't just take my word for it</p>
			<h2 class="big" style="text-align:center; margin: 0 auto 28px;">What teams are saying.</h2>
			<div class="testimonial-placeholder">
				<p>[Testimonial placeholder. Drop a client quote here once you have one, or delete this section. Even one line from a Utah Flag or Hey Bright contact would do a lot of work in this spot.]</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
	-->

	<!-- THE LEGACY SESSION, EXPLAINED -->
	<section class="sec sec-dark">
		<svg class="stripe-mark" style="top: 20px; left: 20px; width: 200px; height: 200px; opacity: 0.4;" viewBox="0 0 200 200">
			<g transform="rotate(-22 100 100)">
				<rect x="20" y="30" width="120" height="14" rx="7" fill="var(--lw-accent)" opacity="0.25"/>
				<rect x="40" y="60" width="140" height="14" rx="7" fill="var(--lw-on-dark)" opacity="0.1"/>
				<rect x="10" y="90" width="90" height="14" rx="7" fill="var(--lw-accent)" opacity="0.15"/>
			</g>
		</svg>
		<div class="content">
			<div class="text-col">
				<p class="eyebrow">How it starts</p>
				<h2 class="big">Start with a conversation. Find the right path forward.</h2>
				<p class="body">The Legacy Session is a complimentary 30&ndash;45 minute conversation designed to uncover what your organization needs next. During our conversation, we'll explore:</p>
			</div>
			<div class="explore-grid">
				<div class="explore-card">
					<h3>Your Legacy</h3>
					<ul>
						<li>Where did your organization come from?</li>
						<li>What traditions, values, and stories define your community?</li>
						<li>What makes your organization unique?</li>
					</ul>
				</div>
				<div class="explore-card">
					<h3>Your Next Era</h3>
					<ul>
						<li>Why are you considering a change right now?</li>
						<li>What do you want your identity to accomplish?</li>
						<li>What would success look like?</li>
					</ul>
				</div>
				<div class="explore-card">
					<h3>Your Opportunities</h3>
					<ul>
						<li>Where is your current identity holding you back?</li>
						<li>What could a stronger brand help you achieve?</li>
					</ul>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="text-col">
				<p class="body" style="margin-top: 8px;">At the end of the conversation, we'll determine the right next step for your organization. That may be a focused identity project, a complete brand transformation, or expanding what you already have.</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- THE THREE PATHS FORWARD -->
	<section class="sec sec-cream offer-section">
		<div class="content">
			<p class="eyebrow">Every organization is at a different stage</p>
			<h2 class="big">Find the right identity solution for your organization.</h2>
			<div class="offer-grid">
				<OfferCard
					href="/services"
					image="/images/services/tier-logo.jpg"
					imageAlt="Utah Yeti primary logo mark, an example of a Legacy Mark project"
					name="Legacy Mark"
					description="A meaningful logo identity built around your organization's story."
				/>
				<OfferCard
					href="/services"
					image="/images/services/tier-system.jpg"
					imageAlt="Utah Yeti full brand system: primary and secondary marks, wordmark lockups, jerseys, number set, and color palette"
					name="Legacy to New Era System"
					description="A complete identity system for organizations entering a new chapter."
				/>
				<OfferCard
					href="/services"
					image="/images/services/tier-identity.jpg"
					imageAlt="Utah Yeti brand identity applied across merchandise and gameday graphics"
					name="Elevate Your Identity"
					description="Bring your identity into uniforms, merchandise, gameday graphics, and beyond."
				/>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- IMAGINE WHAT'S POSSIBLE -->
	<section class="sec sec-dark">
		<div class="content">
			<div class="text-col center">
				<p class="eyebrow">Beyond the field</p>
				<h2 class="big">More than a logo.</h2>
				<div class="imagine-lines">
					<p>The best sports identities don't stay on the field.</p>
					<p>They're worn by families on Saturday mornings.</p>
					<p>Hung as flags outside homes.</p>
					<p>Set as phone wallpapers.</p>
					<p>Printed on hoodies that get passed down.</p>
					<p>Painted on curbs before rivalry games.</p>
					<p>Sometimes they're even tattooed.</p>
					<p>Because when an identity truly represents an organization, it becomes part of the people who support it.</p>
					<p>That's what we're building.</p>
					<p>Not just a logo.</p>
					<p class="imagine-close">An identity people are proud to represent.</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- PROCESS -->
	<section class="sec sec-soft">
		<div class="content">
			<div class="text-col">
				<p class="eyebrow">The Legacy to New Era System</p>
				<h2 class="big">A process built around meaning.</h2>
				<p class="body">Great identities aren't created by jumping straight into design. They're built through understanding, strategy, and intentional decisions.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="phase-row">
				<div class="phase-card"><span class="phase-num">01</span><h3>Discover the Legacy</h3><p>Every project begins by understanding your organization. We uncover your history, culture, traditions, and the qualities that make you unique.</p></div>
				<div class="phase-card"><span class="phase-num">02</span><h3>Define the Identity</h3><p>Research becomes strategy. We identify core themes, visual direction, and creative principles that guide every decision.</p></div>
				<div class="phase-card"><span class="phase-num">03</span><h3>Craft the System</h3><p>Strategy becomes identity. Your logo, visual system, and brand guidelines come together into a cohesive foundation.</p></div>
				<div class="phase-card"><span class="phase-num">04</span><h3>Launch Into a New Era</h3><p>Your identity comes to life. Through presentation, mockups, and rollout guidance, you'll have the tools to introduce your next chapter.</p></div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- WHO YOU'LL WORK WITH -->
	<section class="sec sec-dark">
		<div class="content">
			<div class="nick-split">
				<div class="text-col">
					<p class="eyebrow">Who you'll work with</p>
					<h2 class="big">I'm Nick.</h2>
					<p class="body">I design sports identities for teams and communities entering a new chapter. One studio, one designer, working directly with you start to finish. No account managers, no handoffs.</p>
					<p class="body">My approach is simple: research before design, built for the real world, made to last. I don't design logos for sports teams. I build identities that players wear with pride, fans rally behind, and communities remember.</p>
					<a href="/about" class="btn btn-primary" style="margin-top: 8px;">More about me</a>
				</div>
				<div class="nick-portrait">
					<img src="/images/ProfilePic.JPEG" alt="Nick Holmquist" />
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- IS THIS A FIT -->
	<section class="sec sec-cream">
		<div class="content">
			<p class="eyebrow">Real talk</p>
			<h2 class="big">Is the Legacy Session right for you?</h2>
			<p class="body">This conversation is designed for decision makers at schools, teams, clubs, and leagues who want to build something meaningful.</p>
			<div class="fit-grid">
				<div class="fit-col yes">
					<h3>It's a fit if you</h3>
					<ul class="fit-list">
						<li>Are entering a new chapter and want an identity that reflects where you're going</li>
						<li>Want more than a generic logo or template</li>
						<li>Believe your history, culture, and community are worth representing</li>
						<li>Want to be involved in uncovering what makes your organization unique</li>
						<li>Are looking for an identity built to last</li>
					</ul>
				</div>
				<div class="fit-col no">
					<h3>It's not a fit if you</h3>
					<ul class="fit-list">
						<li>Want to skip discovery and jump straight into concepts</li>
						<li>Are only looking for something copied from a trend</li>
						<li>See branding as just decoration</li>
						<li>Aren't ready to invest time into building something meaningful</li>
					</ul>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- FAQ -->
	<section class="sec sec-soft">
		<div class="content">
			<div class="text-col">
				<p class="eyebrow">Frequently asked questions</p>
				<h2 class="big">Questions answered.</h2>
				<div class="faq-item">
					<h3>Is the Legacy Session really free?</h3>
					<p>Yes. The Legacy Session is a complimentary 30&ndash;45 minute conversation to understand your organization, goals, and opportunities. There is no obligation to move forward. The purpose is to find clarity and determine the right next step.</p>
				</div>
				<div class="faq-item">
					<h3>Do you only work with existing teams?</h3>
					<p>No. The Legacy approach works for both established organizations looking to refresh their identity and new teams looking to create a strong foundation. Every organization has a story worth building from.</p>
				</div>
				<div class="faq-item">
					<h3>What if we don't know exactly what we need?</h3>
					<p>That's exactly what the Legacy Session is for. Many organizations know they want something different but aren't sure what the right solution looks like yet. We'll figure that out together.</p>
				</div>
				<div class="faq-item">
					<h3>How long does the process take?</h3>
					<p>Timelines vary depending on the project scope, organization size, and feedback process. Most complete identity projects take approximately 4&ndash;6 weeks.</p>
				</div>
				<div class="faq-item">
					<h3>Do you only create logos?</h3>
					<p>No. A logo can be the beginning of an identity, but it is only one piece. Depending on your needs, we can create a Legacy Mark, develop a complete Legacy to New Era System, or expand your identity through Elevate Your Identity.</p>
				</div>
				<div class="faq-item">
					<h3>What happens after the Legacy Session?</h3>
					<p>After our conversation, I'll review what we discussed and recommend the best path forward. If we're a good fit, I'll prepare a custom proposal outlining the scope, timeline, and investment. From there, we can begin building your next era.</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- CLOSING CTA -->
	<section class="sec sec-dark closing-band">
		<svg class="stripe-mark" style="bottom: 20px; left: 20px; width: 220px; height: 220px; opacity: 0.45;" viewBox="0 0 200 200">
			<g transform="rotate(-22 100 100)">
				<rect x="10" y="40" width="120" height="14" rx="7" fill="var(--lw-accent)" opacity="0.25"/>
				<rect x="30" y="70" width="150" height="14" rx="7" fill="var(--lw-on-dark)" opacity="0.08"/>
				<rect x="0" y="100" width="90" height="14" rx="7" fill="var(--lw-accent)" opacity="0.15"/>
			</g>
		</svg>
		<div class="content">
			<div class="text-col center">
				<h2 class="big">Ready to discover what's next?</h2>
				<p class="body">Your organization already has a story. Let's create the identity that carries it forward.</p>
				<a href="#start" class="btn btn-primary">Start Your Legacy Session</a>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="lw-start" id="start">
		<div class="content">
			<h2>Start Your Legacy Session</h2>
			<p class="start-sub">Every great identity starts with understanding. Fill out the form below and tell me a little about your organization. This helps me prepare for our conversation and make your Legacy Session as valuable as possible.</p>

			<form class="intake-card" id="intake-form" action="https://formspree.io/f/mgojdjre" method="POST">

				<div class="form-section">
					<h3 class="form-section-title">About Your Organization</h3>

					<div class="field">
						<label for="name">Name</label>
						<input type="text" id="name" name="name" required />
					</div>
					<div class="field">
						<label for="team">Organization / Team Name</label>
						<input type="text" id="team" name="team" required />
					</div>
					<div class="field">
						<label for="email">Email Address</label>
						<input type="email" id="email" name="email" required />
					</div>
					<div class="field">
						<label for="website">Website or Social Links <span class="optional">(optional)</span></label>
						<input type="text" id="website" name="website" />
					</div>
					<div class="field">
						<label>What type of organization are you?</label>
						<div class="radio-group">
							<label class="radio-option"><input type="radio" name="org_type" value="School" required /> School</label>
							<label class="radio-option"><input type="radio" name="org_type" value="Sports Team" /> Sports Team</label>
							<label class="radio-option"><input type="radio" name="org_type" value="League" /> League</label>
							<label class="radio-option"><input type="radio" name="org_type" value="Club" /> Club</label>
							<label class="radio-option"><input type="radio" name="org_type" value="Other" /> Other</label>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>

				<hr class="form-divider" />

				<div class="form-section">
					<h3 class="form-section-title">Your Identity</h3>

					<div class="field">
						<label>What best describes where you are today?</label>
						<div class="radio-group stacked">
							<label class="radio-option"><input type="radio" name="stage" value="Creating a new identity from the ground up" required /> We are creating a new identity from the ground up</label>
							<label class="radio-option"><input type="radio" name="stage" value="Refreshing an existing identity" /> We have an existing identity that needs a refresh</label>
							<label class="radio-option"><input type="radio" name="stage" value="Expanding our current brand presence" /> We want to expand and improve our current brand presence</label>
						</div>
					</div>
					<div class="field">
						<label for="why_now">What's prompting you to look at this now?</label>
						<textarea id="why_now" name="why_now"></textarea>
					</div>
				</div>

				<input type="text" name="_gotcha" class="hp" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" aria-hidden="true" />

				<button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary">Submit Request</button>
				<div class="form-status" id="form-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></div>
			</form>
		</div>
	</section>

	<script>
		(function () {
			const form = document.getElementById('intake-form') as HTMLFormElement | null;
			if (!form) return;
			const status = document.getElementById('form-status');
			const btn = form.querySelector('button[type="submit"]') as HTMLButtonElement;
			const originalBtnHTML = btn.innerHTML;
			if (!status) return;

			form.addEventListener('submit', function (e) {
				e.preventDefault();
				btn.innerHTML = 'Sending...';
				btn.disabled = true;
				btn.style.opacity = '0.7';
				status.className = 'form-status';

				fetch(form.action, {
					method: 'POST',
					body: new FormData(form),
					headers: { Accept: 'application/json' },
				})
					.then(function (response) {
						if (response.ok) {
							form.reset();
							status.className = 'form-status success show';
							status.textContent = "Thanks, your message is on its way. I'll get back to you within a day.";
							btn.innerHTML = originalBtnHTML;
							btn.disabled = false;
							btn.style.opacity = '1';
						} else {
							response.json().then(function (d) {
								let msg = 'Something went wrong. Please email hello@islandtwigstudios.com directly.';
								if (d && d.errors && d.errors.length) {
									msg = d.errors.map((er: { message: string }) => er.message).join(', ');
								}
								status.className = 'form-status error show';
								status.textContent = msg;
								btn.innerHTML = originalBtnHTML;
								btn.disabled = false;
								btn.style.opacity = '1';
							});
						}
					})
					.catch(function () {
						status.className = 'form-status error show';
						status.textContent = 'Something went wrong. Please email hello@islandtwigstudios.com directly.';
						btn.innerHTML = originalBtnHTML;
						btn.disabled = false;
						btn.style.opacity = '1';
					});
			});
		})();
	</script>
</Layout>

<style>
	/* Page-scoped aliases, kept on :global(:root) rather than plain
	   :root: Astro scopes styles per-component, and <html> is
	   rendered by Layout.astro, not this page, so an unscoped-looking
	   :root rule here would silently never match. --lw-strong/--lw-dim
	   are NOT aliased to --text-strong/--text-dim: those are global
	   light-on-dark tokens site-wide, but these are used exclusively
	   for dark text on this page's light surfaces (cream/soft
	   sections, white cards), so they need a fixed dark value
	   regardless of the dark-canvas globals. */
	:global(:root) {
		--lw-bg: var(--bg, #181a19);
		--lw-cream: var(--surface-cream, #f4f1e9);
		--lw-soft: var(--surface-soft, #e8e2d4);
		--lw-accent: var(--accent, #ab8a1f);
		--lw-accent-hover: var(--accent-hover, #8f7219);
		--lw-accent-cool: var(--accent-cool, #2d6b45);
		--lw-accent-bright: var(--accent-bright, #c9a227);
		--lw-on-dark: var(--text-on-dark, #f4f1e9);
		--lw-on-dark-dim: var(--text-on-dark-dim, rgba(244, 241, 233, 0.72));
		--lw-strong: #1a1c1a;
		--lw-dim: #5a5f5a;
		--lw-border-light: var(--border-on-light, #c9c3b4);
		--lw-radius: var(--radius, 12px);
		--lw-radius-sm: var(--radius-sm, 8px);
	}

	.content { position: relative; z-index: 1; max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 48px; }

	.text-col { max-width: 720px; }
	.text-col.center { max-width: 640px; margin: 0 auto; text-align: center; }
	.text-col.center .btn { margin-top: 4px; }

	/* The intake form reads better as a centered column than
	   stretched to the page's full width, matching the same
	   narrower-and-centered treatment used on services.html. */
	.lw-start .content { max-width: 860px; }

	/* .eyebrow is defined in global.css (shared pill, every page). */

	.btn {
		display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: 8px;
		padding: 15px 30px; border-radius: 100px;
		font-size: var(--fs-small); font-weight: 700; text-decoration: none;
		transition: all 0.25s ease; cursor: pointer; border: none;
	}
	.btn-primary { background: var(--lw-accent); color: var(--lw-strong); }
	.btn-primary:hover { background: var(--lw-accent-hover); transform: translateY(-1px); box-shadow: 0 10px 24px var(--shadow-color); }

	.sec { padding: 72px 0; position: relative; overflow: hidden; }
	.sec-dark { background: var(--lw-bg); color: var(--lw-on-dark); }
	.sec-cream { background: var(--lw-cream); color: var(--lw-strong); }
	.sec-soft { background: var(--lw-soft); color: var(--lw-strong); }

	h2.big {
		font-size: var(--fs-h2); font-weight: 700;
		letter-spacing: -0.01em; line-height: 1.25; margin-bottom: 18px;
	}
	.sec p.body { font-size: var(--fs-body-lg); line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 16px; }
	.sec-dark p.body { color: var(--lw-on-dark-dim); }
	.sec-cream p.body, .sec-soft p.body { color: var(--lw-dim); }
	.sec p.body:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

	.lw-hero { background: var(--lw-bg); padding: 52px 0 80px; position: relative; overflow: hidden; }

	/* overflow: visible since the rotated rects inside can extend a
	   few units past the 200x200 viewBox on some corners — SVGs clip
	   to their viewBox by default, which was cutting a sliver off a
	   rounded end. */
	.stripe-mark { position: absolute; pointer-events: none; z-index: 0; overflow: visible; }

	.hero-grid {
		position: relative;
		z-index: 1;
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 1.1fr 0.9fr;
